{"step_index":190,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-13T19:11:59Z","thinking":"Discovered baseline discounts at Vijay Sales, typically 5-8% off standard MacBook Pro configurations. Croma offers Tata Neu Coins (5% with specific credit card) along with potential instant discounts and exchange bonuses. Reliance Digital also has deals.\n\n\nFocusing on credit card offers, specifically September 2026, to identify optimal instant discount strategies for MacBook Pro purchases in India. HDFC EMI offers tiered discounts, with a maximum of ₹15,000 for purchases over ₹2,50,000. American Express and OneCard offer larger capped discounts, potentially better for high-value configurations. HSBC provides discounts at Vijay Sales, while IDFC and ICICI have percentage-based discounts. The availability of custom configurations (32GB or CTO models) might be limited to store orders.\n\n\nAnalyzing additional discount strategies, including Apple's official store cashback offers with HDFC and Amex. Examining retailer exchange bonuses at Vijay Sales and Croma, integrated with third-party services. Evaluating Apple Trade In and Cashify's direct buyback offers for trade-in value optimization.\n\nConsidering open-box and display model deals from Sahivalue, noting the potential for significant discounts, including CTO configurations, to find the best total savings opportunity. The potential for the greatest discount lies between trade-in offers and open-box options.\n\n\nExploring refurbished and pre-owned options: Cashify, Amazon Renewed, CeX, Electronic Bazaar, and ControlZ offer varying warranties and grading. CeX provides the longest warranty at 24 months.\n\nConsidering Apple Premium Partners (APRs) like Unicorn Store, Aptronix, Imagine, Maple, and iVenus for potentially better deals. APRs often discount previous-generation Apple Silicon models significantly, unlike the Apple Store which quickly discontinues them.\n\n\nConsidering a brand-new 